pipeline {
    agent any

    parameters {
        string(name: 'CLUSTER_ID', defaultValue: '', description: 'Cluster ID to check')
        string(name: 'LOOKBACK_DAYS', defaultValue: '6', description: 'Days to look back')
    }

    environment {
        PATH = "${env.HOME}/.local/bin/backplane/latest:${env.HOME}/.local/bin:/usr/local/bin:${env.PATH}"
    }

    stages {
        stage('Checkout') {
            steps {
                checkout scm
            }
        }

        stage('Backplane Login') {
            steps {
                script {
                    echo "Setting up Backplane authentication..."
                    if (!params.CLUSTER_ID) {
                        error("CLUSTER_ID parameter is required")
                    }
                    sh """
                        export PATH=\${HOME}/.local/bin/backplane/latest:\${PATH}
                        ocm backplane login ${params.CLUSTER_ID}
                    """
                    echo "✅ Backplane login successful"
                }
            }
        }

        stage('Setup') {
            steps {
                sh 'chmod +x scripts/*.sh utils/*.sh'
            }
        }

        stage('Check OOM Events') {
            steps {
                script {
                    def results = sh(
                        script: "./scripts/check-oom-events.sh ${params.LOOKBACK_DAYS}",
                        returnStdout: true
                    ).trim()

                    if (results) {
                        echo "⚠️  Found OOMKilled events"

                        // Build detailed Service Log message
                        def oomCount = results.split('\n').size()
                        def message = """Out of Memory (OOM) Events Detected

SUMMARY:
Found ${oomCount} OOMKilled event(s) in the last ${params.LOOKBACK_DAYS} days.

OOM EVENTS:
"""

                        results.split('\n').each { line ->
                            def parts = line.split('\\|')
                            def namespace = parts[0]
                            def podName = parts[1]
                            def ageDays = parts[2]
                            def timestamp = parts[3]

                            message += """
• Namespace: ${namespace}
  Pod: ${podName}
  Occurred: ${ageDays} day(s) ago
  Timestamp: ${timestamp}
  Reason: Container exceeded memory limit
"""
                        }

                        message += """
IMPACT:
OOMKilled pods indicate:
- Insufficient memory allocation for workload
- Potential memory leaks in application
- Service interruptions and restarts
- Data loss if application doesn't persist state
- Degraded performance before OOM occurs

ROOT CAUSE ANALYSIS:
1. Review current memory limits:
   'oc get pod <pod> -n <namespace> -o jsonpath="{.spec.containers[*].resources}"'

2. Check actual memory usage before OOM:
   - Review metrics in Prometheus/Grafana
   - Query: container_memory_usage_bytes

3. Analyze application logs for memory patterns:
   'oc logs <pod> -n <namespace> --previous'

RECOMMENDED ACTIONS:
1. Increase memory limits if workload legitimately needs more:
   'oc set resources deployment/<name> -n <namespace> --limits=memory=1Gi --requests=memory=512Mi'

2. For memory leaks:
   - Review application code
   - Check for unbounded caches/collections
   - Implement proper garbage collection
   - Add memory profiling

3. Optimize application memory usage:
   - Review buffer sizes
   - Implement streaming for large data
   - Use pagination for database queries
   - Clear unused objects/connections

4. Set appropriate requests and limits:
   - requests: typical usage
   - limits: maximum allowed (prevents runaway)
   - Gap between them allows burst usage

CAPACITY PLANNING:
Monitor memory trends over 7-30 days to set appropriate limits with headroom.

SEVERITY: Warning
Memory issues can cause service instability and data loss.
"""

                        echo message

                        sh """
                            // Write message to temporary file to avoid argument length issues
                            writeFile file: 'service-log-message.txt', text: message

                            sh """
                                cat service-log-message.txt | ./utils/send-service-log.sh '\${params.CLUSTER_ID}' 'Warning' 'OOMKilled Events Detected (${oomCount} occurrences)'
                            """
                        """

                        currentBuild.result = 'UNSTABLE'
                    } else {
                        echo "✅ No OOMKilled events in last ${params.LOOKBACK_DAYS} days"

                        // Build positive Service Log message
                        def message = """Memory Health Check - No OOM Issues Detected

SUMMARY:
No Out of Memory (OOM) events detected in the last ${params.LOOKBACK_DAYS} days. All pods are running within their memory allocations.

MEMORY STATUS:
✅ No OOMKilled events in the last ${params.LOOKBACK_DAYS} days
✅ All pods running within memory limits
✅ No memory pressure issues detected

VERIFICATION PERFORMED:
• Scanned cluster events for OOMKilling events
• Reviewed pod termination reasons across all namespaces
• Verified no containers exceeded memory limits

MEMORY HEALTH INDICATORS:
• Container memory limits are appropriately sized
• Applications managing memory efficiently
• No memory leaks or excessive consumption patterns detected

NEXT STEPS:
✅ No action required - memory health is good
✅ Continue regular monitoring
✅ Next automated check will run in 6 days

MONITORING DETAILS:
• Check Type: Automated OOM Event Detection
• Lookback Period: ${params.LOOKBACK_DAYS} days
• Check Date: ${new Date().format('yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss')} UTC
• Next Check: Scheduled in 6 days

SEVERITY: Info
This is a routine memory health confirmation. No OOM issues detected.
"""

                        echo message

                        sh """
                            // Write message to temporary file to avoid argument length issues
                            writeFile file: 'service-log-message.txt', text: message

                            sh """
                                cat service-log-message.txt | ./utils/send-service-log.sh '\${params.CLUSTER_ID}' 'Info' 'Memory Health Check - No OOM Issues Detected'
                            """
                        """

                        currentBuild.result = 'SUCCESS'
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }

    post {
        always {
            script {
                sh '''
                    export PATH=${HOME}/.local/bin/backplane/latest:${PATH}
                    ocm backplane logout || true
                '''
                echo "🔒 Backplane session closed"
            }
        }
        failure {
            echo "❌ Pipeline failed - check cluster access"
        }
        success {
            echo "✅ OOM events check completed successfully"
        }
    }
}
